These data details the trajectories of 6 surface drifters deployed with and without drogue during a regular sea survey campaign referred to as "PELLETS" 

Two types of drifters were used: 

- Type 1 (pellet1, pellet2 and pellet3): Type 1 are are a set of cylinder-shaped home-made drifters without drogue.
For more details about this type of buoys, please visit: https://doi.org/10.5194/os-18-1703-2022
- Type 2 (pellet4, pellet5 and pellet6): Type 2 are a set of cylinder-shaped home-made drifters with drogue.
These buoys were equipped with an anchor of 0.5 m long positioned in the water column between 0.8 and 1.3 m depth, allowing them to drift with surface currents. 

Reference time: local

To get a first look at the trajectories, visit: https://aztidata.es/ebegi/ (Platform type: "Drifters")
